{% comment %}
    Renders the add-to-cart drawer: full-height panel sliding in from the
    right, showing cart contents, an optional cross-sell, and checkout CTAs.
    Body content lives in cart-notification-content and is re-rendered on
    every add-to-cart via sections/cart-notification-product.liquid.

    Accepts:
    - color_scheme: {String} sets the color scheme of the drawer (optional)

    Usage:
    {% render 'cart-notification' %}
{% endcomment %}

<cart-notification style="display: none;">
  <div class="cart-drawer__overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div
    id="cart-notification"
    class="cart-drawer{% if color_scheme %} color-{{ color_scheme }}{% endif %} focus-inset"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-label="{{ 'general.cart.item_added' | t }}"
    role="dialog"
    tabindex="-1"
    inert
  >
    <div class="cart-drawer__header">
      <h2 class="cart-drawer__heading">{{ 'sections.cart.title' | t }}</h2>
      <button type="button" class="cart-drawer__close focus-inset" aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}">
        {{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}
        <svg class="icon icon-close" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#icon-close"></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div id="cart-notification-content" class="cart-drawer__body">
      {% render 'cart-notification-content' %}
    </div>
  </div>
</cart-notification>

{% comment %}
  Critical inline styles: the component stylesheet loads async, so without
  these the drawer flashes unstyled (in page flow, giant checkmark icon)
  on every navigation until the CSS arrives. No visibility:hidden here —
  it would out-specify the stylesheet and keep the drawer's layer
  unrasterized (see the note in component-cart-notification.css); the
  transform alone keeps it off screen.

  Position alone was not enough. cart-notification.js is deferred, so it
  clears the element's display well before the async stylesheet lands,
  and in that window the panel had no width, height or background: a
  transparent, content-sized block of cart markup parked just past the
  right edge. Nothing overflows — the document is never wider than the
  viewport — but a trackpad's horizontal overscroll bounces past the edge
  and shows it, until the stylesheet arrives and turns it into a tidy
  white panel. These values mirror the stylesheet exactly, so the drawer
  is the same shape from the first paint.
{% endcomment %}
{% style %}
  /* Same reservation the stylesheet makes; critical too, so the viewport
     width does not change under the page when the stylesheet lands. */
  html {
    scrollbar-gutter: stable;
  }
  cart-notification .cart-drawer {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 100%;
    height: 100dvh;
    width: min(48rem, 100vw);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background-color: rgb(var(--color-background, 255, 255, 255));
    z-index: 9999;
    transform: translateX(100%);
  }
  cart-notification .cart-drawer__overlay {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
{% endstyle %}
